     1	# Apple UI-test and screenshot validation
     2	
     3	This is the reusable UI-validation foundation for the macOS client and the
     4	shared iOS Simulator proof. It is deliberately isolated from production tunnel
     5	behavior: the two fixture hosts have no dependency on NetworkExtension, either
     6	platform adapter, the packet-tunnel provider, VPN preferences, credentials, or
     7	network clients.
     8	
     9	## Source and target ownership
    10	
    11	`ReluxAppleUITestShared` is the single source of truth for accessibility
    12	identifiers, timeout values, typed launch keys, and deterministic fixture names.
    13	The macOS containing app imports the module as a compile-time integration anchor;
    14	both fixture hosts and both UI-test targets consume the same package product.
    15	Raw `RELUX_UI_TEST_*` keys are confined to
    16	`ReluxUITestLaunchConfiguration.swift` and checked by
    17	`scripts/check-apple-ui-test-contract.py`.
    18	
    19	The generated test-only target graph is:
    20	
    21	```text
    22	ReluxProxyMacUITests -> ReluxProxyMacUITestFixtureHost -> ReluxAppleUITestShared
    23	ReluxProxyIOSUITests -> ReluxProxyIOSUITestFixtureHost -> ReluxAppleUITestShared
    24	```
    25	
    26	The dormant production `ReluxProxyIOS` and `ReluxProxyIOSTunnel` targets remain
    27	deferred. The iOS target above is a simulator-safe fixture host, not resumed
    28	product scope. Neither UI-test scheme embeds or builds a packet-tunnel provider.
    29	
    30	`ReluxUITest.PageElement`, `ComponentElement`, `PageManager`, and
    31	`Page.FixtureHost` are shared by the two UI-test targets. Page methods describe
    32	the expected state or action (`waitForAppearance`, `waitForFixture`,
    33	`confirmFixture`) and synchronize with `waitForExistence` or XCTest predicate
    34	expectations. Fixed wall-clock sleeps are prohibited by the contract check.
    35	
    36	## Deterministic fixture launch
    37	
    38	Construct only `ReluxUITest.LaunchConfiguration(fixture:)`. It generates the
    39	complete launch arguments and environment; tests and scripts must not spell raw
    40	keys independently. Parsing fails closed unless the current schema, a known
    41	fixture, UI-test mode, and the `disabled` network boundary are all present.
    42	
    43	The fixture matrix covers:
    44	
    45	- profile: empty, configured;
    46	- trust: unknown, approved, changed, revoked;
    47	- capability: available, unavailable;
    48	- failure: authentication, transport, relay;
    49	- diagnostic: empty, populated;
    50	- onboarding: required, complete;
    51	- migration: required, complete;
    52	- privacy: redacted.
    53	
    54	Every value is a deterministic non-secret enum case. The fixture host renders
    55	only public labels and cannot connect, mutate VPN preferences, request system
    56	extension or NetworkExtension approval, or bypass a production safety decision.
    57	
    58	## Smoke, xcresult, extraction, and diffs
    59	
    60	Run the focused contract gate first:
    61	
    62	```bash
    63	make apple-ui-test-contract
    64	```
    65	
    66	Run the complete build-host gate and a controlled snapshot mismatch with:
    67	
    68	```bash
    69	make apple-ui-test-smoke
    70	```
    71	
    72	Each invocation creates a unique directory below
    73	`.temp/TASK-260715-1idq8c/apple-ui-test/`. The native macOS row performs an
    74	unsigned `build-for-testing`, retains its Xcode log and `.xctestrun` product
    75	inventory, and does not launch the app or test runner. The iOS Simulator row
    76	runs the smoke, writes an `.xcresult` and Xcode log, then passes the result to
    77	`scripts/extract_apple_ui_test_artifacts.py`. The extractor exports only
    78	`Step_*` PNG attachments into test-specific directories and writes
    79	`screenshots.json`. The runtime row then independently validates that manifest,
    80	requires non-empty PNG files for both expected smoke steps, and propagates any
    81	extractor or validation failure to the aggregate gate. The focused contract
    82	gate includes an injected extractor-failure regression against the production
    83	smoke script.
    84	
    85	The controlled mismatch invokes `relux-snapshot-diff`. An image mismatch is the
    86	expected exit code `1` and must produce the three review files
    87	`reference.png`, `failed.png`, and `diff.png`. Exit `0` means the images match;
    88	exit `2` means the comparison could not be performed. Product-screen SwiftUI
    89	snapshot suites are intentionally not added before product screens exist; the
    90	diff engine and Swift Testing artifact suite establish the failure workflow
    91	without inventing business UI.
    92	
    93	This workstation keeps `CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO` and
    94	`CODE_SIGNING_REQUIRED=NO`. The iOS Simulator row can run unsigned. Native
    95	macOS runtime proof is explicitly deferred to `TASK-260822-3q4grm` on the
    96	dedicated signed test host. `summary.txt` records that owner and distinguishes
    97	the successful native macOS build-for-testing row from the deferred runtime
    98	row. Do not sign, install, or launch the native fixture here to make that row
    99	look complete.
   100	
   101	## Mandatory visual review
   102	
   103	Extraction is not acceptance. A human or reviewing agent must open every
   104	step-named PNG and record a result for all four checks:
   105	
   106	| Check | Required evidence |
   107	| --- | --- |
   108	| Orientation | expected portrait/landscape orientation; no rotation or sideways content |
   109	| Layout | content uses the expected viewport; no clipped, collapsed, or corner-squashed UI |
   110	| Content | required state labels/actions are present and readable |
   111	| Rendering | image is not empty, black, frozen on launch, or otherwise missing the app UI |
   112	
   113	Record the inspected filenames, destination, and pass/fail findings in the
   114	task-scoped outcome. A passing test process without this review is incomplete.
   115	
   116	## Separate physical-device evidence contract
   117	
   118	Physical-device-only evidence is never inferred from Simulator, native Mac, or
   119	unsigned build results. Each later physical row must attach a separate resource
   120	named `TASK-<row-id>_physical-apple-ui-evidence.md` and a task-scoped artifact
   121	directory containing:
   122	
   123	- device class/model and OS/build (identifier redacted to a non-reversible
   124	  suffix or lane-local alias);
   125	- exact authorized test command, destination class, scheme, test identifier,
   126	  and exit code;
   127	- `.xcresult`, extracted step screenshots, and `screenshots.json`;
   128	- the four-field visual review above for every screenshot;
   129	- signing/provisioning lane name without certificate, profile, Keychain, UDID,
   130	  credential, or secret bytes;
   131	- explicit statement whether the row is fixture-only or separately authorized
   132	  for product/system VPN behavior.
   133	
   134	Any row that installs or launches the product/provider, requests approval,
   135	creates or changes VPN preferences, or exercises real routing/DNS/tunnel state
   136	belongs to its named physical security gate and must not be run under this
   137	fixture smoke contract. Designed-for-iPad Mac is not a UI-test destination.
